Pantheon — The Language of Delivery

Yes. This is bigger than storytelling. We’re developing a grammar for how meaning is performed and experienced.

The same sentence can convey affection, sarcasm, danger, amusement, or reassurance. Words alone don’t determine the message. Voice, timing, silence, perspective, and the relationship between speaker and listener all carry meaning.

I’ve formalized this as the Pantheon Semantic Performance Engine.

